{#
  name: disclosure (helper, not a component)
  purpose: The open and close motion every <details> shares (R-MOT-06): the content grows and fades in when it opens and shrinks and fades out when it closes.
  anatomy: one class on a <details> element, defined as an @utility in engine/theme/app.css (R-PREC-07): `disclosure` (accordions, menu groups) or `disclosure-tabs` (tab sets that stack as an accordion below md)
  variants: accordion (height and opacity) | tabs (height and opacity below md; a fade-in only at md and up, where two panels must never stand stacked during a switch)
  states: closed (height 0, clipped, transparent) | open (height auto, opaque)
  spacing: none; the content keeps its own padding inside the clipped box
  motion: 300 ms on --ease-reveal; content-visibility transitions as a discrete property so closing animates before the content is hidden; height to and from auto works because <html> carries interpolate-size: allow-keywords. Browsers without ::details-content or interpolate-size open and close instantly. Reduced motion: instant (the transition sits in a no-preference media query inside the utility).
  keyboard: native details and summary
  a11y: native
  i18n: none
  content limits: none
  why a utility: written as utilities on each element the pattern cost about 500 bytes per <details>, and every page carries three in the mobile menu (R-PERF-01)
#}
{% macro disclosure(variant="accordion") %} {{ "disclosure-tabs" if variant == "tabs" else "disclosure" }}{% endmacro %}
